multiplexing  serial  communications  interface For 4‐port TC‐400
series boards: For 8‐port TC‐800 series boards: The  driver  pro‐
vides  support for the Byte Runner Technologies TC‐400 and TC‐800
series boards that multiplex together up to four or eight  commu‐
nications interfaces.  Each device is the master device for up to
eight  devices.  The kernel configuration specifies these devices
as slave devices of the device, as shown in  the  synopsis.   The
slave ID given for each device determines which bit in the inter‐
rupt  multiplexing register is tested to find interrupts for that
device.  The specification for the device is used to compute  the
base  addresses for the subdevices and the port for the interrupt
multiplexing register.  Not all  possible  configuration  options
are  currently  supported (for example, speeds beyond 115200 baud
are not currently supported).  The driver was  written  by  Jukka
Marin.
